    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d191">

                <pb facs="0271" n="259" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg259"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390.1115A/676: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Rangoon</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Schnare</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rangoon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-01-31T13:00:00+06:30">January 31, 1942—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 31—11:26 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>106. Referring to the Department’s telegram No. 51, December 20, second
                        paragraph.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d191-f1"/> When full emergency capacity of
                    vessel within number of life preservers available not needed for American
                    citizens and their families may persons of other nationalities be covered by
                    emergency certificates?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schnare</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
